WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.200
The 8.9 mile gap between the European and
African continent known as the Straight of

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.710
Gibraltar is home to multiple strange territories
and borders.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:17.930
On the European side, there is a 2.6 square
mile British Overseas territory named Gibraltar.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.640
This means that Britain shares a small land
border with Spain.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.380
On the African side of the straight is the
Spanish city of Ceuta, separated completely

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.070
from the rest of Spain.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.220
This city is an autonomous community within
Spain, essentially having similar rights as

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.320
the independent regions that make up Spain.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.240
A little more than 100 miles down the African
coast is Melilla, another Spanish exclave

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.710
in northern Africa.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.489
All this means that Spain shares significant
land borders with Morocco, and that in effect

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:48.309
only one country separates British soil from
African soil.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:51.590
Two other European countries also have strange
border relations.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.960
Conventional wisdom would say that the Netherlands
and France do not share a land border.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.692
Belgium stands between the two countries,
however, on the other side of the world, the

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:00.659
two countries do share a border.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:05.159
The Caribbean island of Saint Martin is split
between a French collectivity, Saint Martin,

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:09.750
and a Dutch constituent country, Sint Maarten,
meaning that you can walk from France to the

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.840
Netherlands without crossing through another
country.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.880
Also part of France is French Guiana.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.500
French Guiana has the exact same political
power as any other French department and region

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.049
despite being on the other side of the Atlantic
Ocean.

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:27.219
It has a comparable relationship as Hawaii
to the United States—geographically separated

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.000
but politically integrated.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.710
This means that France shares a land border
with both Brazil and Suriname.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.210
There are two daily flights from French Guiana
to Paris which make for one of the longest

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.090
domestic flights in the world.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:44.789
These flights take off in France and land
in France, but take 9 hours and cross 4,401

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:46.229
miles.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:49.299
Despite this, this is not the longest domestic
flight in the world.

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:53.909
The longest is also within France and goes
from Paris to the French overseas department

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:56.780
of Réunion, located in the Indian Ocean.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.909
The flight is 5,809 miles long and takes just
over 11 hours.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:06.200
And over to North America, it’s impossible
to walk or drive from New York to LA without

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.659
crossing over water.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:11.780
The Saint Lawrence river connects the Great
Lakes to the Atlantic Ocean, then the Chicago

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:16.030
River connects to the Des Plaines River which
connects to the Illinois River which connects

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.440
to the Mississippi River which flows out into
the Gulf of Mexico.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.720
It’s also impossible to go from the South
to the North of the US without crossing water.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.150
Theres one creek in the Teton wilderness of
Wyoming that divides at a place called the

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.799
Parting of the Waters.

00:02:30.799 --> 00:02:39.010
One side flows 3,488 miles to the Atlantic
while the other 1,353 to the Pacific.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.110
This means that this is one of the few natural
waterways connecting the Atlantic to the Pacific.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.760
Near those great lakes that make up part of
the water split is Middle Island, Canada,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.630
the southernmost point in Canada.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:57.480
A majority of US states—27—actually lie
fully or partially north of this point.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:03.470
The closest point in Europe to the US is the
Dingle Peninsula in Ireland, only 2539 miles

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.129
away from Hamill, Maine.

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.940
The island of Ireland is politically divided
between the autonomous country of the Republic

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.480
of Ireland and the section of Great Britain,
called Northern Ireland.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.540
Although, despite the name, the northernmost
part of the island of Ireland is not in Northern

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.689
Ireland; it’s Malin Head, part of the Republic
of Ireland.

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:22.900
Now to finish it off we’ll head up to Norway.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.800
Norway's land stretches over Sweden and Finland
to actually shares a border with Russia.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.760
On the other side of Eurasia, Russia also
shares a tiny 11 mile border with North Korea.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.920
This means that only one country separates
the Nordic social democracy in Norway from

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:54.229
the communist dictatorship of North Korea.

